  Europe PMC abstract: the nonlocal periodic code lets an ideal observer estimate location with a robustness to noise outside the class of observed sensory and motor population codes; a simple network can correct it.

CROSSREF 200  10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000291  2009  PLoS Computational Biology
  Burak, Y.; Fiete, I. R.  Accurate Path Integration in Continuous Attractor Network Models of Grid Cells.
  Europe PMC abstract: continuous attractor models can integrate velocity and heading; with spike variability the simulated networks integrate on the order of 10–100 m and 1–10 min. Not used as a heat result.

CROSSREF 200  10.1162/neco_a_00319  2012  Neural Computation
  Mathis, A.; Herz, A. V. M.; Stemmler, M.  Optimal Population Codes for Space: Grid Cells Outperform Place Cells.
  Europe PMC abstract: place cells spike at one location, grid cells at the sites of a hexagonal lattice; under Fisher information and at low spike counts, optimized grid codes beat place codes for spatial resolution, with a tradeoff against spatial range. Nested modules, more short spacings than long ones, and a self-similar field-to-period ratio are predicted.

